{"step_index":42,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-31T12:51:11Z","content":"Bhai, ekdum simple bhasha mein samajh. Look at the image I just generated above.\n\nImagine kar tu apne bedroom mein betha hai aur room mein heater chal raha hai. Kamre ki hawa (Inside Air) bohot garam hai. \n\nLekin wo heat directly sheeshe (glass) ke andar nahi hai. Wo heat pehle room ki **hawa (fluid)** mein float kar rahi hai. (Yeh red wavy arrows hain image mein).\n\nAb us heat ko bahar nikalna hai. Toh heat kya karegi? Wo hawa se ja kar sheeshe ki surface (solid) par takrayegi. \n\nHeat ka yeh jo safar hai—**Hawa se Solid tak takrana**—isi ko hum **Convection** bolte hain. Aur yeh free mein nahi hota. Hawa se solid mein ghusne mein heat ko thodi mushkil (rukawat) hoti hai. Usi rukawat ko hum **Convection Resistance ($R_{conv} = \\frac{1}{hA}$)** bolte hain. \n\nMere \"jump\" bolne ka matlab tha ki heat ek **fluid (hawa)** medium se ek **solid (glass)** medium mein \"jump\" maar rahi hai. Jab bhi heat fluid se solid (ya solid se fluid) mein jati hai, wahan Convection hota hai.\n\n**Ek aur relatable example:**\nJab tu garam chai (hot tea) cup mein dalta hai, toh chai ke andar conduction hota hai. Par chai ke upar jo hawa hai, wahan heat chai (liquid) se hawa (gas) mein \"jump\" maarti hai. Isliye tu phook (blow) maar ke usko aur jaldi thanda karta hai. Wo phook maarna convection ko badhata hai!\n\nWindow wale question mein:\n1. Garam Hawa $\\rightarrow$ Glass (Yeh first jump hai = Inside Air Convection)\n2. Glass ke andar travel karna (Yeh Conduction hai)\n3. Glass $\\rightarrow$ Bahar ki thandi hawa (Yeh second jump hai = Outside Air Convection)\n\nAb clear hua ki \"Inside Air\" ka resistor kyu lagaya tha starting mein?"}
